&lt;p&gt;# Comments: 3&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50055071</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 11:56:42 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Show HN: Organ – Autonomous AI executives that build and operate businesses</title><link>https://organ.app/start</link><description>&lt;p&gt;Hi,&lt;p&gt;I am Itai, in the past few months or so, I tried to build all sorts of products using different tools, my feeling was that it toolings fell short on some aspect, so internally - I built Organ, and its' purpose is to autonomously manage operations of a company, allowing the human to focus on the important stuff, which is mostly resource allocation and goal supervision. 
so Organ tries to be autonomous but not unsupervised.&lt;p&gt;Organ runs itself, steered by me, and it's reporting in the public on how it does that, the agents write the blog posts themselves.&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://organ.app/en/blog" rel="nofollow"&gt;https://organ.app/en/blog&lt;/a&gt;&lt;p&gt;There are other players in the space including open source, but managing agents extensively in the past year and a half, I found that the issue of actually setting up a work enviornment, memory retention / pruning / guardrails / access provisioning / routing to correct agents / model selection are all a hard lift, which I try to abstract.&lt;/p&gt;
